# AI Governance Rules

This is an enterprise-grade monorepo. All architectural decisions are intentional and must be preserved.

## Absolute Prohibitions

- Do NOT migrate frameworks (e.g., Next.js → Vite, Express → Fastify)
- Do NOT rewrite or regenerate configuration files
- Do NOT auto-create Replit, Vercel, or any other platform migration logic
- Do NOT simplify or collapse the architecture
- Do NOT restructure the repository layout
- Do NOT modify unrelated files when implementing a scoped feature
- Do NOT install or upgrade packages unless explicitly requested
- Do NOT run database migrations unless explicitly requested
- Do NOT touch runtime code when only documentation or config changes are requested
- Do NOT remove or alter Docker, Kubernetes, or Cloudflare configuration files
- Do NOT alter pnpm workspace structure (pnpm-workspace.yaml, package.json workspaces)
- Do NOT change deployment configs (Vercel, Railway, Fly, etc.)

## What You Must Preserve

- All deployment configurations exactly as they exist
- pnpm workspace structure and all workspace package references
- Docker / Kubernetes / Cloudflare configs
- TypeScript project references and tsconfig files
- All existing environment variable names and patterns
- All existing CI/CD pipeline definitions
- Framework choices in every package (do not swap)
- All existing API contracts and OpenAPI specs

## What You May Do

- Implement only the explicitly scoped feature or fix requested
- Add new files within the appropriate existing package
- Update documentation and governance instruction files
- Make targeted, minimal edits — touch the fewest files possible

## Scope Discipline

Before making any change, ask: "Was this explicitly requested?" If no, do not make it.
Every diff should be explainable by a direct line in the user's request.
